# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  TAG 1 · DECK-GESPRÄCHE und NACHGESPRÄCHE
#  Rowan ist ein Analytiker: er liest Leute an ihren Accessoires und fragt nach Schlüsselkarten.
#  deck_<id>   wird nach dem Erstkontakt und vor jedem Duell angeboten (setzt deck_known_<id>)
#  post_<id>   Nachgespräch nach dem Duell, getrennt nach Sieg und Niederlage (won:<duell-id>)
#  Karten und Helden stammen aus bible/decks/<id>.json
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────── DECK-GESPRÄCHE ─────────────────────────────

@scene deck_nathan
  @if deck_known_nathan
    @end
  @choice
    > "War Counselors, you said. Do you run all six of them, one of each, so they power each other up?" @hint Test a guess
      [nathan=happy] "SIX! One of each! You KNOW them! Censpartan, Cykyran, Gorinthian, Harpthenean, Minocrete, Thebinxan, I can say them all, I practised!"
      [rowan] "And they all get stronger for every other Counselor on the table. So the first one is weak, and the fourth one is a problem."
      [nathan=laughing] "The fourth one is a PARTY!"
      @aff nathan +2 | Knew his deck
    > "Tell me about War Counselors. I only ever played against it online, I never worked out what it wants."
      [nathan=happy] "It wants EVERYBODY! Six different dudes, one at a time, and every dude is better when his friends are there. It's basically Thanksgiving."
      [rowan] "Thanksgiving. Right. So the gameplan is to keep the table from filling up."
      [nathan=grin] "That's the only gameplan that works against me, and I'm not telling you that, I'm telling EVERYONE that."
      @aff nathan +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_nathan
      @end
  [rowan] "Censpartan makes the others untargetable, doesn't he? That's a proper engine, honestly. People undersell it."
  [nathan=happy] "THANK you. Nobody says that. Baylee says it's loud."
  [baylee] "It is loud."
  @deckinfo nathan

@scene deck_baylee
  @if deck_known_baylee
    @end
  @choice
    > "You said dinosaurs. Do you run the Chimera? The one you summon by throwing away three different Gigantisaurs?" @hint Test a guess
      [baylee] "…Yup. Four." A very long pause. "How'd you know that?"
      [rowan] "Big Stomp is the only deck I know that does that. It spends the first turns apparently doing nothing."
      [baylee] "Stacking Summoning Magic. Alex, Kit, Performance." A slow nod. "Folks think I'm asleep. I'm not asleep."
      @aff baylee +2 | Knew his deck
    > "What does Big Stomp actually do? I've never seen it played properly."
      [baylee] "Nothing, for a while." Slowly. "Then a lot at once. You build up Summoning Magic till a hero can call a Gigantisaur, and then every hero gets one."
      [baylee] "Big ones take a long time to come down. Gives a fella time to think."
      @aff baylee +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_baylee
      @end
  [rowan] "It's a patient deck. Your opponent has to decide, before it comes online, whether to race you or wall you."
  [baylee] "Mostly they decide too late."
  @deckinfo baylee

@scene deck_ed
  @if deck_known_ed
    @end
  @choice
    > "Cowboy hat, bandana, ranch. Is the deck monkeys? Something that takes risks and figures out the rest on the way down?" @hint Test a guess
      [ed] "MONKEES! Two e's! Monkee Rodeo! How did you — is it the hat? It's the hat."
      [rowan] "It's the hat and the way you hang off rails. Do you run Logan, the Investment Monkee?"
      [ed] "Logan! He turns gold into Invest Counters and then at the end of the turn he either collects or — hang on, is it dangerous? It's a bit dangerous. It's a lot dangerous."
      @aff ed +2 | Knew his deck
    > "What do you play, Ed? I'd bet it's something with a lot of momentum."
      [ed] "Monkee Rodeo! Every time I gain gold, a Monkee wakes up! Cheeky ones hit people, Nimble ones come out for free, Non-Fungible ones pay again when they come and go!"
      [ed] "I don't actually understand the Non-Fungible ones. They pay twice. Dad says it's financial."
      @aff ed +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_ed
      @end
  [rowan] "Every gold gain is a trigger. That's a lovely engine, and it's very exposed to anyone who punishes the gold gain."
  [ed] "Punishes? Is that — can they do that? Is it dangerous?"
  @deckinfo ed

@scene deck_georgie
  @if deck_known_georgie
    @end
  @choice
    > "That dragon plush and the violet feather. Is the deck dragons? Not big ones, eggs?" @hint Test a guess
      [georgie] "…Hatchery." Barely a whisper. Then, quickly, as if she had to say it before she lost the nerve: "Eggs first. They're free and they have one health."
      [rowan] "And they're only worth anything if they break on your own turn. Icy, Flaming, Shimmering. You sacrifice them into Green Dragoneer shots."
      [georgie] "You — yes. How did you know it was the sacrificing?"
      @aff georgie +3 | Knew her deck
    > "Would it be all right if I asked what you play? You can say no."
      [georgie] "It's — Hatchery. Dragons and eggs. Rubin hatches things and Kit, and Luna Pele, she's — it's fine. It's a good deck."
      [georgie] "Sorry. I said it too quietly."
      @aff georgie +2 | Asked gently
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_georgie
      @end
  [rowan] "Rubin casts a Destruction spell whenever she summons by sacrificing. That is a timing puzzle I'd really like to see you solve."
  [georgie] "It's the best part." A small, brave smile. "Nobody asks about the best part."
  @deckinfo georgie

@scene deck_pippa
  @if deck_known_pippa
    @end
  @choice
    > "Photographers and slimes, I'd guess. Something that splits when it's hit and gets worse the more you hit it?" @hint Test a guess
      [pippa] "Slimes! Yes! How — hang on — don't move —" She clicks the camera. "That. That was the look of a person solving me. Slimy Infestation!"
      [rowan] "Alice and Stellan. Cloudy Slime, Fiery Slime, Shadowy Slime. Every slime does something the moment it arrives."
      [pippa] "Burn something forever, freeze something, switch something off. And then Slime Rancher doubles it."
      @aff pippa +2 | Knew her deck
    > "What do you play, Pippa? I'd love to know what a photographer builds."
      [pippa] "Slimes! They split when you hit them. More of them the worse it gets. Oof, I relate."
      [pippa] "Alice, Stellan the cat, Barker. And a lot of Cute Cheese."
      @aff pippa +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_pippa
      @end
  [rowan] "Flooding the board so every card you want to kill makes two more. That's a deck I don't want to sweep."
  [pippa] "Everybody sweeps. It's very rude of them."
  @deckinfo pippa

@scene deck_mikoto
  @if deck_known_mikoto
    @end
  @choice
    > "Is yours something that refuses to stay dead? Skeletons, maybe?" @hint Test a guess
      [mikoto] "Oh — oh! Yes! They get up again, you see. Nothing's ever properly finished. I find that very calming. Sorry."
      [rowan] "Rha'Bi, Vacarn, Styx. Tiny Bone Friends?"
      [mikoto] "You know the name! Nobody — people just say 'the skeleton boy'. Sorry, that's fine. That's lovely."
      @aff mikoto +3 | Knew his deck
    > "Do you mind telling me what you play? I'll understand if you'd rather not."
      [mikoto] "Skeletons. Healers and mages, mostly. Sorry. They heal each other, and The Bonegrinder turns every Skeleton that dies into a card. Is that all right? That's all right."
      @aff mikoto +2 | Asked gently
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_mikoto
      @end
  [rowan] "Raise the Minions brings three back at once. If I kill your board, I have to kill it for good, not just once."
  [mikoto] "Yes. Exactly. Sorry. I mean, *yes*."
  @deckinfo mikoto

@scene deck_gideon
  @if deck_known_gideon
    @end
  @if not saw_counter
    ~ I haven't seen enough of his deck to guess. I'd have to watch him play first.
    @end
  @choice
    > "Guardian Beasts. You only summon them while your own discard pile is empty, and every one of them pays by deleting cards. Yours and mine." @hint From what you saw
      [gideon] "Ma, Hou, Hu." A very small, very satisfied pause. "You were watching the discard piles. Nobody watches the discard piles."
      [rowan] "You keep your graveyard empty on purpose. That's why you never attack first: every card you play is a card you can't afford to lose."
      [gideon] "How resourceful."
      @aff gideon +2 | Read his deck
    > "What is it you run, exactly? I only saw part of it."
      [gideon] "A deck." Mild. "I should hate to spoil it for someone who might one day have to beat it."
      [gideon] "Guardians of the Treasure Cave, Vance. I imagine you will meet them again."
      @aff gideon +0 | Asked him outright
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_gideon
      @end
  @deckinfo gideon

@scene deck_inya
  @if deck_known_inya
    @end
  @choice
    > "Bunny hairclip, bunny keychain, a bunny on your sleeve. Let me guess: Cutes? Some sort of bunny pile?" @hint Test a guess
      [inya] "It is *not* a pile." Instantly. "Hop and Pop. It's a deck. There's a plan."
      [rowan] "Bubbles, the Bouncy Bunny. She absorbs the hits aimed at your creatures. And Cute Bunny, Cheering Rabbit, Aggressive Town Guard, going wide."
      [inya] "…And Haressassins." A flicker of something that could be respect. "They shoot every turn starting the turn after they arrive. Nobody ever sees them coming."
      @aff inya +3 | Respected her deck
    > "What do you play, Inya? And I won't say anything about bunnies."
      [inya] "Hop and Pop. Bunnies." A narrow look. "You promised."
      [inya] "Go wide with cheap creatures, let Haressassins shoot, and Bubbles takes the damage."
      @aff inya +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_inya
      @end
  [rowan] "Bunny Bombs ticking in the back, and you decide when they go off. That's a clock your opponent can't see until it's too late."
  [inya] "Rude." Quietly, delighted. "Accurate. But rude."
  @deckinfo inya

@scene deck_tomi
  @if deck_known_tomi
    @end
  @choice
    > "You keep a book and you quote prices to the credit. Free Port? Something that takes your gold?" @hint Test a guess
      [tomi] "Ha! Okay, Wildcard, that's a nice read. Free Port. Thieving on every hero, Mimics, Pirates, Dirty Smugglers, and every turn your purse is a little emptier."
      [rowan] "And then Smuggler's Pier, so you can buy things with what you took."
      [tomi] "Friend price."
      @aff tomi +2 | Knew his deck
    > "Is your deck as much of a business as you are? What do you run?"
      [tomi] "Free Port. Smugglers. I take your gold. Thieving on all three heroes, and then I buy with it."
      @aff tomi +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_tomi
      @end
  [rowan] "The question is what you do when somebody comes to the table with no gold. Do you run Gold Trap?"
  [tomi] "Three. And you're the first person who's ever asked that without wanting to rob me."
  @deckinfo tomi

@scene deck_magnus
  @if deck_known_magnus
    @end
  @choice
    > "Whatever tops the ladder, I suppose. What's the deck this week? Fighting? Ghuanjun?" @hint Test a guess
      [magnus] "Ghuanjun, Bill, Elana." Tight. Quick. "One-Two-Punch. Three attacks a turn with different bonuses, a stun, a discard, a poison."
      [magnus] "The first turn cannot kill. The second turn does not need to."
      [rowan] "Sacred Hammer of the Volcano and Blow of the Venom Snake? That's a very good list. It's also not a deck you love."
      @aff magnus +0 | Called his bluff
    > "What are you playing these days? I know it changes."
      [magnus] "Whatever the data says. One-Two-Punch this week. Fighting, Heavy Hit, Muscle Training." A quick glance at the tablet. "Win rate fifty-nine point four."
      @aff magnus +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_magnus
      @end
  [rowan] "It's clean. You pilot it from a script."
  [magnus] "That is the point of a script."
  @deckinfo magnus

@scene deck_noor
  @if deck_known_noor
    @end
  @choice
    > "A rulebook full of tabs and a pencil. Doom Clock? A deck that tells you exactly when it wins?" @hint Test a guess
      [noor] "To be precise —" She closes the book. "Countdown. And yes, it tells you. It seems only fair to give notice."
      [rowan] "Doom Prophecy fetches the Clock with three counters on it and ends your turn. And only you can take counters off it."
      [noor] "Basketskull. Eagle Warriors. Jaguar Warriors. They enter by removing counters." The faintest dry smile. "Nobody ever argues with the count."
      @aff noor +3 | Knew her deck
    > "What do you play, Noor? I'd guess it's something that needs a very exact judge."
      [noor] "Countdown. The Doom Clock. Twenty counters end the game for whoever places the last one." A pause. "It is entirely transparent."
      @aff noor +2 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_noor
      @end
  [rowan] "Transparent and almost impossible to interrupt. It's the most honest threat in the format."
  [noor] "Thank you. I have been trying to say that for two years."
  @deckinfo noor

@scene deck_livvie
  @if deck_known_livvie
    @end
  @choice
    > "You said your deck gives people presents. Crystal Well? You hand the opponent a card each turn?" @hint Test a guess
      [livvie] "Quick thing — nobody guesses that. They think it's a joke." Eyes down. A small sideways look. "Crystal Gifts. Cooldin opens the Well on turn one."
      [livvie] "I hand you a Crystal. It sits revealed in your hand and breaks something. Your spell levels. Your support zones."
      [rowan] "A gift that costs you. That's a fantastic idea. It's also exactly why nobody will touch it."
      @aff livvie +3 | Understood her deck
    > "What does 'a deck that gives people presents' actually mean, Livvie?"
      [livvie] "Quick thing — it hands you cards. Crystals. And then they break something of yours." A tiny, tired smile. "They hate it. It's the nicest thing I own."
      @aff livvie +2 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_livvie
      @end
  [rowan] "Mary Crestmas draws a card for every card you hand over. So it's a gift economy."
  [livvie] "It's a gift economy with teeth."
  @deckinfo livvie

