# ───────────────────────────── NACHGESPRÄCHE ─────────────────────────────

@scene post_baylee
  @if won:ferry_baylee
    Baylee turns his hand over, one big dinosaur at a time, and studies the board.
    [baylee] "You didn't attack at all."
    [rowan] "I waited until you'd stacked your Summoning Magic and then I killed the hero that would have called the Chimera. You never got to call it."
    [baylee] "Huh." Slowly. "Good animal, that one. Big. Never got out of the barn."
    [rowan] "If I'd let the Chimera land I'd have lost. It's the best card in your deck."
    [baylee] "Don't tell Nathan I said that. He'd put it on a T-shirt."
  @else
    Baylee sets down his last giant. It is, you notice, almost apologetic.
    [baylee] "Sorry. Chimera came down on turn six."
    [rowan] "I should have killed Alex when he was still doing nothing. Everything else was built around him."
    [baylee] "That's right." Pleased, and visibly embarrassed about being pleased. "You'd have to get him early. Most folks don't."
    [baylee] "Your storm's something, though. Hit three of my big ones at once. I'd not seen that."
  @aff baylee +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_ed
  @if won:ferry_ed
    Ed is flat on his back on the planks with his hat on his chest, grinning at the sky.
    [ed] "Whoa. I didn't see the Storm come back around. It just — kept zapping! Every turn! Is that allowed?"
    [rowan] "That's the whole deck. Gathering Storm attaches to a hero and keeps hitting three of your targets at the start of every turn."
    [ed] "Three! Every turn! My bananas didn't stand a chance." He sits up. "I gained a lot of gold, though. Did you see how much gold I gained?"
    [rowan] "I saw. If I hadn't destroyed Logan, that bank would have woken every Monkee at once."
  @else
    Ed leaps up and does a lap of the rail, hat held on with one hand.
    [ed] "I WON! Did you see Logan? Did you see how much gold? It was like a bank robbery but the other way!"
    [rowan] "You gained gold on three different turns and a Monkee woke up every time. I couldn't keep up."
    [ed] "That's the whole deck!" He grins. "It's a good deck, right? It wasn't just the hat."
    [rowan] "It wasn't the hat. Although the hat helps."
  @aff ed +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_georgie
  @if won:ferry_georgie
    Georgie is looking at her last egg, which is still unbroken. She has gone very quiet.
    [georgie] "I couldn't break it. They only pay when they break on my turn, and you never let me have a turn where it mattered."
    [rowan] "I killed Rubin before she could sacrifice. If she'd survived one more turn the eggs would have broken in your favour."
    [georgie] "You noticed Rubin." A very small voice. "Usually they notice the dragons."
    [rowan] "The dragons are just what she throws."
    A tiny, astonished smile.
    [georgie] "That's — yes. That's what Pippa says."
  @else
    Georgie has already stacked her cards into a tidy pile and is holding Ember, the green plush dragon, on her knee.
    [georgie] "Sorry."
    [rowan] "You don't have to say sorry."
    [georgie] "I always do. I can't stop." A pause. "You attacked on turn four. I thought you'd attack on turn three."
    [rowan] "I wanted to see whether you'd break an egg early. You didn't, and then it was too late for me."
    [georgie] "Everyone breaks an egg early." She looks at her hands. "You're the first person who waited."
  @aff georgie +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_mikoto
  @if won:ferry_mikoto
    Mikoto is looking at the board with wide, unfocused eyes. A skeleton at the bottom of his discard pile has not quite finished falling over.
    [mikoto] "Sorry — oh. Sorry. You killed all my healers before they could heal anything. I didn't — that's — that's good. That's what you should do."
    [rowan] "I went after the Necromancer first. If he'd survived, Raise the Minions would have brought three back."
    [mikoto] "It would have! It would have, wouldn't it? I had it in my hand!" A giggle, then quick embarrassment. "Sorry. It was a very good plan."
  @else
    Mikoto stares at his board, and then at you, and then bursts into a breathless laugh that is half relief.
    [mikoto] "I won! I'm sorry, I'm so — I won. The Bonegrinder came down on turn five and it turned every skeleton you killed into a card."
    [rowan] "I should have left them alone. Every time I killed one I was drawing for you."
    [mikoto] "Nothing's ever properly finished." Quietly, for him. "That's — I've been trying to say that for years."
