@scene post_sunny
  @if won:ferry_sunny
    Sunny is still on her face on the planks, counting push-ups aloud, and then rolls over with a grin and a towel on her face.
    [sunny] "Ten! No dramas! Nobody told me you'd go for the Whoolmoth first."
    [rowan] "It was the only card that could slide into three of my heroes. If it landed, I'd have lost."
    [sunny] "It never landed. Clever." She sits up. "I like your storm. It doesn't slide. It just waits."
  @else
    You are lying next to a seagull on your back, arms burning. Sunny rolls onto her side, propping her head on one hand.
    [sunny] "That was a proper game! Everything slides, and you kept the Spikeblock off your Hero for four turns. That's hard."
    [rowan] "I couldn't stop the Snowman, though. That froze me in position for a turn and I couldn't use the spell."
    [sunny] "That's the trick." Cheerfully. "You can't stop everything. You can only choose what hurts less."
